  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 118 AM EST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nThe next system to impact our region will be a quick moving \nshortwave ejecting out of the SW US towards the Gulf on Tuesday and \nthen moving towards the eastern Gulf on Wednesday. Another frontal \nboundary and weak low will approach the area by mid week. Increased \nmoisture will result in scattered showers and thunderstorms on \nTuesday and Wednesday, with Wednesday looking to be the most active \nday of the week. PWAT values on Wednesday increase to 1.8-2.0 inches \nand depending on the track of the low some locally heavy rain may \noccur in portions of the area, especially SE FL. The shortwave axis \nswings through the area by late Wednesday into early Thursday which \nwill kick the frontal boundary well off to our east, and drier air \nwill return to the area for the end of the work week. \n\nTemperatures through the end of the work week and into the beginning \nof next weekend will be fairly consistent with highs in the upper \n70s to lower 80s each day, and low temps generally in the 60s.",
